{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Store accepts secret-bearing event bodies; leak blocked all tickets pushes\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nAt 2026-08-03 19:13 an agent session posted a comment on ticket 129e containing a full zsh\nenvironment dump. The dump embedded SEVEN live credentials (Anthropic, 2x GitHub PAT,\nGemini/Google, Jira/Atlassian, OpenAI service-account, PyPI). GitHub push protection then\nrejected `refs/heads/tickets` (GH013) on the Anthropic key, so EVERY session's store writes\nqueued local-only — 153 commits at diagnosis. One comment caused a full store-sharing outage\nfor all concurrent agents, and it presented as transient contention: the only symptom was\n`WARNING rebar._store.push: tickets branch push failed after 3 retries`.\n\nThis is urgent now because the store auto-pushes to a single shared ref, so any agent that\npastes an environment dump into a comment wedges the branch for everyone until a human\nintervenes.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThere is no content screening anywhere in the write path. `_store/event_append._validate_event`\n(`src/rebar/_store/event_append.py:126`) checks the envelope shape and `event_type` membership\nonly, and never inspects `data`. Confirmed RED before any fix: `leaf.comment(<ticket>,\n\"KEY=<live-shaped anthropic key>\")` returns 0 and the COMMENT event lands on disk.\n\nCorollary the original diagnosis got wrong, and which this plan corrects: `append_event` is NOT\nthe single write seam. `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_translate.py:258-276` writes\nJira-sourced COMMENT/EDIT bodies — untrusted EXTERNAL input — by calling the halves of\n`finalize_event` directly, deliberately bypassing `append_event` because that helper\ncommits+pushes eagerly. The txn and delete cores bypass it too. A screen at `append_event` would\ntherefore have left a credential pasted into a Jira comment able to reproduce this exact wedge.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd a deterministic, pure secret screen and enforce it at `_seam.finalize_event`\n(`src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py:329`) — the one function `append_event`\n(`src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py:405`), the txn/delete cores, and the reconciler's inbound\ntranslate all route through. Inbound translate is changed to call the seam rather than its\nhalves, and a test pins that routing so it cannot regress into a bypass again.\n\nOn a match the write is REFUSED — the event does not land — per the operator decision recorded\non this ticket (2026-08-07). Redaction was considered and rejected: silently rewriting a\ncaller's payload makes the stored event differ from what the caller believes it wrote, and in an\nappend-only store that divergence is unrecoverable after the fact. Refusal is loud, reversible,\nand leaves the caller in control. A force override (`--allow-secret-pattern=<reason>`) keeps a\nfalse positive from ever being a permanent hard block; it is the same escape-hatch shape as\n`--force-close`, is CLI-only (never exposed over MCP), and records who forced and why on the\nevent itself so a forced write is auditable.\n\nRefusal must be safe to leave ON by default, which drives two design constraints:\n\n- It names WHICH family fired and WHERE (field + line), so using the override is an informed\n  choice rather than a blind retry.\n- It never echoes the secret. `SecretFinding` (`src/rebar/secret_screen.py:116`) carries\n  family/field/line and structurally has NO value field, so the value cannot leak through the\n  refusal message, logs, stderr, or the event on disk. Payload dict KEYS are redacted before\n  they reach the printed field path, since a credential used as a key would otherwise leak\n  through the path itself.\n\nDetection is tuned by measurement against the live store rather than by argument. Patterns match\na FIXED-WIDTH window rather than a greedy `{80,}` quantifier, so same-class padding appended\nafter a real key (400 `-` characters — an ASCII rule in a log or env dump) cannot dilute the\nentropy average below the floor and make the screen miss a genuine credential. The PEM pattern is\nline-anchored, because a real paste puts the banner on its own line whereas prose enumerating\nbanners does not.\n\n`llm/workflow/lint.py` consumes the shared pattern table instead of keeping a second copy, which\nhad already drifted — it lacked the Anthropic/OpenAI/Atlassian/PyPI families the incident\nactually carried.\n\n## Scope\n\nRecorded via `set-file-impact` (paths). New: `src/rebar/secret_screen.py` (pattern table, pure\n`scan_text`/`screen_event_data`, override audit record, refusal message) and\n`tests/unit/test_secret_screen_e7a9.py`. Modified: `src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py` (enforce at\n`finalize_event`), `src/rebar/_commands/__init__.py` (parse the override above BOTH dispatch\nroutes so every write verb honours it, not just `comment`), `src/rebar/_commands/leaf.py` and\n`src/rebar/_lib_writes.py` (thread the override through), `src/rebar/llm/workflow/lint.py`\n(consume the shared table), `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_translate.py` (route\nthrough the seam), `docs/user-guide.md` (the command-substitution hazard + the screen/override).\n\nOut of scope: surfacing the GH013 push-rejection detail. That was bug 2a76 and already landed on\nmain (`tests/unit/test_push_rejection_surfacing.py`); AC5 below records it rather than\nduplicating it.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Fire: each of the families the incident dump carried is refused, asserted via the family name\n  in the refusal. Credential-shaped fixtures are ASSEMBLED AT RUNTIME (`_fake_secret`,\n  `_pem_banner`) so this repo never commits a live-shaped literal and the repo's own secret\n  scanner stays fully armed on the test file.\n- No-fire: the verbatim benign strings the live-store sweep found — a truncated placeholder\n  (`sk-ant-api03-...`), a regex literal (`sk-ant-api03-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{93,}`), and prose\n  enumerating PEM banners — all still write.\n- Padding: a real key followed by 400 same-class padding characters is still refused (the\n  fixed-width-window regression).\n- No-echo: the secret value AND its head/tail fragments are absent from five channels — the\n  exception message, stdout, stderr, the log records, and every byte on disk. The forced-write\n  path is checked separately because it is the only path that logs, so asserting on log records\n  in the refusal path alone would be vacuous. A positive control proves the on-disk assertion\n  can actually observe a landed value.\n- Bypass: a test pins that the reconciler's inbound translate routes through `finalize_event`,\n  and another pins that the override is absent from the MCP surface.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] A write whose event data matches a high-confidence credential pattern is REFUSED at\n      `_seam.finalize_event` and the event file does not exist on disk afterwards — verified by\n      a test that asserts the command's non-zero exit and the absence of the event.\n- [x] The refusal names the matched secret family and the field+line, and does NOT echo the\n      secret value — verified by asserting the value and its head/tail fragments are absent from\n      the exception message, stdout, stderr, log records, and all on-disk bytes.\n- [x] Benign look-alike text (truncated placeholders, regex literals, prose enumerating\n      banners — the verbatim strings from the live-store sweep) still writes successfully, so\n      the screen is safe to leave on by default — verified by explicit negative-case tests.\n- [x] The screen covers writers that do NOT go through `append_event`, specifically the\n      reconciler's inbound Jira translate — verified by a test asserting inbound translate\n      routes through `finalize_event`.\n- [x] `--allow-secret-pattern=<reason>` allows the refused write for every write verb, records\n      the reason and bypassed families on the event, and is absent from the MCP tool surface —\n      verified by tests over the CLI verbs and a test asserting MCP non-exposure.\n- [x] The shell command-substitution hazard that produced the incident is documented in\n      `docs/user-guide.md` with the exact wrong and right forms.\n- [x] The incident is recorded on this ticket with its blast radius, including that the only\n      control which actually stopped the leak (GitHub push protection) was outside this project.\n- [x] Surfacing the GH013 push-rejection reason is confirmed ALREADY satisfied on main by bug\n      2a76 (`tests/unit/test_push_rejection_surfacing.py`) and is not duplicated here.\n\n## Absorbed from e4f4 (closed as duplicate)\n\ne4f4-295b-2c03-44c4 described the same underlying defect (the store accepting secret-bearing\nevent bodies) and was filed about 8 minutes apart from this ticket with no link between them.\nIts two ACs with no counterpart here — documenting the shell command-substitution hazard for\nagents, and recording the incident with its blast radius — are folded into the Acceptance\nCriteria above so nothing is lost by closing it."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786105210996565001,"uuid":"5898ac46-9c87-4c90-8127-2786de6900c7"}